From f6f0d37cd6173f88b3132f5c038a222a2a449f1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:05:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: remove an unreachable door-count test from
 borg_play_step()

On breeder levels borg_play_step() closes an adjacent open door before
moving.  Its scan skipped every door when track_door.num >= 255, under
the comment "Skip repeatedly closed doors".  track_door holds 100
entries and its count only grows while it is below that size, so the
test is never true; it is also a count of the whole list, not a test of
the door being looked at.

Remove the test and its comment.  No behaviour change.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#126.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow.c b/src/borg/borg-flow.c
index 948675159..78fef9b28 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow.c
@@ -639,10 +639,6 @@ static bool borg_play_step(int y2, int x2)
                 if (ag->kill)
                     continue;
 
-                /* Skip repeatedly closed doors */
-                if (track_door.num >= 255)
-                    continue;
-
                 /* skip our original goal */
                 if ((oy + borg.c.y == y2) && (ox + borg.c.x == x2))
                     continue;
-- 
